    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a gross back year release of GBP 20.4m in 2023 for the 2021 closed year of account and prior years, representing a 3.42% release of opening gross reserves. This favorable development was driven by releases in long-tail casualty classes (GBP 7.0m gross), short-tail accounts (GBP 6.6m gross), and the auto account for 2019 and 2020 years (GBP 6.7m gross) due to benign experience. Further releases resulted from the resolution of an outstanding dispute related to Superstorm Sandy and the removal of specific IBNR for stable 2019 events like Hurricane Dorian and Japanese windstorms. Litigation related to Covid-19 also developed favorably. However, there was some adverse development from 2020 wind events (Hurricane Laura, Hurricane Sally, Derecho) and a small deterioration in the 2003 casualty account.",
